## JAVA IMPLEMENTATION — What Exists (Read-Only)

> This section documents the Java codebase as it stands. **Do not modify any file under
> `java_logic/`.** This section exists so the AI understands what the Java code does —
> not so it copies it into Python.

### Java: Overall Architecture
The Java app follows a strict **MVC + Observer** pattern with JavaFX for the GUI.

- `Main.java` launches the JavaFX `Application`.
- `AppLauncher` (the JavaFX `Application` subclass) prompts the user to select two CSV
  files (campers, then classes) via system file-chooser dialogs, constructs the model and
  controller, and opens the main window.
- `ModelImpl` notifies all registered `ModelObserver`s whenever `sortCampers()` or
  `closeProgram()` is called.

### Java: Model Layer (`java_logic/main/java/org/class_sorter/model/`)

**`Camper` interface / `CamperImpl` class**

Fields held internally by `CamperImpl`:
- `String firstName`, `String lastName`
- `int age`
- `String cabin`
- `boolean canShoot`
- `List<String> prefs` — ordered list of up to 6 class-name strings representing the
  camper's ranked preferences
- `List<Class_> classes` — all classes the camper is currently enrolled in
- `Class_ classA`, `classB`, `classC`, `classD` — individual per-slot assignments

Key behaviors in `CamperImpl`:
- `assignClassA/B/C/D(Class_ cl)` — assigns the camper to the given slot and
  simultaneously registers the camper in the class's enrollment list for that slot.
- `cleanPrefs(List<Class_> classesList)` — removes duplicate entries from `prefs`, then
  pads the list to 6 entries by appending randomly selected classes not already in the
  list.
- All public mutators throw `IllegalArgumentException` on null arguments.

**`Class_` interface / `ClassImpl` class**

(`Class_` uses a trailing underscore because `class` is a reserved word in Java.)

Fields held internally by `ClassImpl`:
- `String name`
- `int A_capacity`, `B_capacity`, `C_capacity`, `D_capacity` — independent capacity per
  slot
- `List<Camper> enrolled_A`, `enrolled_B`, `enrolled_C`, `enrolled_D` — independent
  enrollment list per slot
- `List<Camper> firstPrefs` — campers whose current top preference is this class
- `boolean requiresShootingForm`

Key behaviors in `ClassImpl`:
- `getCapacity(int section)` — `section` is **0-indexed** (0=A, 1=B, 2=C, 3=D).
- `getNumEnrolled(int i)` / `getCampersEnrolled(int i)` — `i` is **1-indexed**
  (1=A, 2=B, 3=C, 4=D). *(Note: the indexing convention differs from `getCapacity` —
  this is an inconsistency in the Java code itself.)*
- `enrollCamper(Camper camper)` — randomly picks a slot number (0–3), checks that the
  slot is open and the camper meets the shooting requirement, then assigns the camper.
  Returns an integer status code: 1–4 = assigned to that slot, 5 = class entirely full,
  6 = failed after retry limit, 7 = shooting form required but camper ineligible.
- `isFull(int i)` — 1-indexed; returns true when a slot's enrollment count equals its
  capacity.
- `isEnrolled(Camper camper)` — checks all four slot references.

**`Model` interface / `ModelImpl` class**

State held by `ModelImpl`:
- `ArrayList<Camper> campers`
- `ArrayList<Class_> classes`
- `List<ModelObserver> observers`
- `boolean areCampersSorted`, `boolean isProgramDone`

Key behaviors:
- `createCampers(File file)` / `createClasses(File file)` — delegates to `Factory`.
- `sortCampers()` — runs up to 10 rounds. Each round: call `setFirstPrefs()` to populate
  each class's `firstPrefs` list → iterate over classes and enroll each camper in their
  `firstPrefs` list → call `cleanPrefs()` on every camper. Notifies observers when done.
- `closeProgram()` — sets `isProgramDone = true` and notifies observers.

**`ModelObserver` interface**

Single method: `void update(Model model)`. Implemented by any class that needs to react
to model state changes.

**`Factory` class**

- `createCampers(File)` — uses `Scanner` with delimiter pattern `,|\r\n|\t`; skips the
  first 11 header tokens; then reads per camper: `lastName` (String), `firstName`
  (String), `age` (int), `cabin` (String), `canShoot` (String "True"/"true"/"TRUE" →
  boolean), followed by 6 preference strings.
- `createClasses(File)` — uses `Scanner` with delimiter `,|\r\n`; skips the first 6
  header tokens; then reads per class: `name` (String), `A_Capacity`, `B_Capacity`,
  `C_Capacity`, `D_Capacity` (all int), `requiresShootingForm` (String → boolean).

### Java: Controller Layer (`java_logic/main/java/org/class_sorter/controller/`)

**`Controller` interface / `ControllerImpl` class**

`ControllerImpl` holds a reference to `Model` and a `String name` (the user-chosen
output file name; defaults to a success message string).

Every method is a thin delegation to the model, with one exception:
- `getFileName()` / `setFileName(String)` — manages the output file name string locally
  within the controller; not delegated to the model.
- All other methods (`getCampers`, `getClasses`, `getSortedCampers`, `getIsSorted`,
  `getIsProgramDone`, `createCampers`, `createClasses`, `sortCampers`, `closeProgram`)
  pass directly through to the model.

### Java: View Layer (`java_logic/main/java/org/class_sorter/view/`)

**`FXComponent` interface**
Single method: `Parent render()`. All visual components implement this.

**`AppLauncher`** (extends `Application`)
- Shows two sequential `Alert` dialogs to prompt the user to select CSV files via
  `FileChooser`.
- Constructs `ModelImpl`, calls `createCampers` and `createClasses`, then calls
  `cleanPrefs` on every camper.
- Constructs `ControllerImpl` and `PromptView`, sets up the JavaFX `Scene`.
- Registers a lambda `ModelObserver` that calls `promptView.render()` and resizes the
  stage on every model update.

**`View`** (implements `FXComponent`, `ModelObserver`)
- Wraps `PromptView` in a `BorderPane` with padding.
- `update(Model model)` delegates to `render()`.

**`PromptView`** (extends `Node`, implements `FXComponent`, `ModelObserver`)
- Before sorting: renders a `TextField` for the output file name and a button labelled
  "Click to sort into Classes!"
- On button click: calls `controller.getSortedCampers()` (which triggers the sort), then
  writes a CSV to the working directory with columns:
  `Last Name, First Name, Cabin, Class A, Class B, Class C, Class D`.
  Outputs the literal string `"ERROR1"` in a slot column when the camper's slot is null.
- After sorting: renders the output file name and a location hint for the user.

### Java: Tests (`java_logic/test/java/org/class_sorter/AppTest.java`)
- `instantiateTest()` — manually constructs classes and campers with hardcoded data;
  makes no assertions (smoke test only).
- `csvTest0()` / `csvTest1()` — load campers/classes from hardcoded absolute paths
  (`/Users/connorhitchings/Desktop/...`). These paths do not work on any other machine
  and are an example of what **not** to do.
- `sortTest0()` — loads both CSVs, runs `getSortedCampers()`, prints results, and throws
  `RuntimeException` if any camper ends up with zero class assignments.

